title: Radek's Salon
subtitle: In Moabit prison, Moscow's man receives visitors.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 8 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Hungarian Soviet Republic falls; Romanian troops in Budapest', 3);
!}

= Radek's Salon

On 1 August the Hungarian Soviet Republic fell, and Romanian troops are in Budapest. In Moabit Karl Radek has been moved to a comfortable cell. The government wants a channel to Moscow, and his visitors now include industrialists, diplomats and nationalist officers as well as our own comrades.

Radek agrees with [+ party_chair +] that the party must stand in elections and work in the unions. He also thinks that throwing out the Left Radicals would cost the party its best fighters. He offers to write to the coming congress.

- @theses: Ask him to write for the Zentrale's theses.
- @unity: Ask him to argue for unity above all.
- @keep_out: Keep Radek out of the party's affairs.
- @join: Join the International through Radek.

@theses
subtitle: Moscow's name behind the theses. The letter will have a second half we did not ask for.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_radek = 1;
Q.independence -= 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction -= 4;
RG.ecci('radek', 8);
!}

@unity
subtitle: The Left Radicals will start quoting him.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_radek = 2;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 3;
RG.ecci('radek', 6);
!}

@keep_out
subtitle: The party's quarrels are German quarrels. Radek will remember.
on-arrival: {!
Q.heid_radek = 0;
Q.independence += 5;
RG.ecci('radek', -10);
!}

In Moabit Radek turns back to his industrialists.

@join
subtitle: The party becomes a section of the International, like everyone else.
view-if: comintern_member = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.comintern_member = 1;
Q.independence -= 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 8);
RG.ecci('radek', 5);
RG.news('German party joins the Communist International', 3);
!}
